{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLHarmony\/Chord-swift.struct\/Kind-swift.struct"},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLHarmonyV5ChordV4KindV","roleHeading":"Structure","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Kind","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Kind","kind":"identifier"}],"extendedModule":"IvorMXL","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"title":"MXLHarmony.Chord.Kind"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Kind indicates the type of chord. Degree elements can then add, subtract, or alter from these starting points."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Kind"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The attributes are used to indicate the formatting of the symbol. Since the kind element is the constant in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"all the harmony-chord groups that can make up a polychord, many formatting attributes are here."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The use-symbols attribute is yes if the kind should be represented when possible with harmony symbols rather"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than letters and numbers. These symbols include:"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"major: a triangle, like Unicode 25B3 minor: -, like Unicode 002D augmented: +, like Unicode 002B diminished:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"°, like Unicode 00B0 half-diminished: ø, like Unicode 00F8"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For the major-minor kind, only the minor symbol is used when use-symbols is yes. The major symbol is set using"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the symbol attribute in the degree-value element. The corresponding degree-alter value will usually be 0 in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this case."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The text attribute describes how the kind should be spelled in a score. If use-symbols is yes, the value of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the text attribute follows the symbol. The stack-degrees attribute is yes if the degree elements should be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stacked above each other. The parentheses-degrees attribute is yes if all the degrees should be in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parentheses. The bracket-degrees attribute is yes if all the degrees should be in a bracket. If not specified,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"these values are implementation-specific. The alignment attributes are for the entire harmony-chord group of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which this kind element is a part."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The text attribute may use strings such as “13sus” that refer to both the kind and one or more degree"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements. In this case, the corresponding degree elements should have the print-object attribute set to “no”"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to keep redundant alterations from being displayed."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLHarmony\/Chord-swift.struct\/Kind-swift.struct\/init(value:usesSymbols:text:areDegreesStacked:areDegreesInParentheses:areDegreesBracketed:position:font:color:halign:valign:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers"},{"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\